  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Suppose that we wish to find the equation of the **horizontal line** that passes through the point $(0,3)$, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14166027/assets/379af2ba930fa537f1fbdda5b4b5cc91e355a46e90918cdc56bbce66f3502d7b.png)\n\nNotice that for *any* $x$-value on the line, the $y$-value is always $\\color{red}3.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14166027/assets/ff5ec246a558fc981ba5f0b0085ce3663ac6ab837121f31a5d44de6adb91cb90.png)\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is $y=3.$\n\n**Note**: When writing the equation of a horizontal line, we always put the variable $y$ on the left side and the constant on the right side.",
